WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.133
Forgetting and Leitner boxes.

2
00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:11.400
Memory fades by the same fraction each stretch of days. Stability S is how many days until recall drops to ninety percent.

3
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.133
Bigger stability, slower forgetting.

4
00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:24.967
Now review on days one, three, seven and fourteen. Each review resets recall to the top, and boosts stability, so the next dip is shallower.

5
00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:30.200
Without reviews, the grey curve: most of it is gone in a month.

6
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:41.000
The classic rule: six boxes with growing gaps. A correct answer moves the card up a box. A wrong answer sends it back to box zero.

7
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.500
Right, right, right, then one slip, and it falls all the way back.

8
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:53.367
Leitner is strong. But on our simulated students it keeps ninety-nine percent of easy concepts, and only eighty-one percent of hard ones.

9
00:00:53.367 --> 00:01:00.900
One fixed ladder can't fit every concept. A policy that adapts could do better, and that's what we'll train.

